From: glaziermag <glaziermag@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tls: send the second request once in the post-handshake auth test

Upstream: https://github.com/secdev/scapy/commit/c5e9a5b0cd25f4d0bb87c3b208db342edea7da38

The test called send() and then sr1() for the same request. The server can
reply to the first copy and close while the client is still sending. The
client then misses the queued response. Let sr1() send the request once
and wait for the response. The test still requires the body "Welcome".

--- a/test/scapy/layers/tls/tlsclientserver.uts
+++ b/test/scapy/layers/tls/tlsclientserver.uts
@@ -525,7 +525,6 @@
     pkt = a.sr1(REQS[0], timeout=1, verbose=0)
     assert pkt.load == b"Please login"
     # Second request
-    a.send(REQS[1])
     pkt = a.sr1(REQS[1], timeout=1, verbose=0)
     assert pkt.load == b"Welcome"
     # Close
